plan.rationale:
In commit 841816a8c ('mmu: preserve global TLB entries on an ASID-scoped sfence.vma'), Wally added ASID-scoped TLB invalidation filtering to preserve global (PTE_G=1) translations when an sfence is scoped to a specific ASID. The commit introduced `sfencevmaAllM` in `src/privileged/privdec.sv` and plumbed it as `TLBFlushAll` to the instruction and data MMU/TLB modules. However, two compounding functional defects exist in the implementation of the Svinval standard extension:

1. Privileged Decoder Defect (src/privileged/privdec.sv line 86):
   The decoder computes:
     assign sfencevmaAllM = sfencevmaM & ~|InstrM[24:20];
   This assumes that `InstrM[24:20]` is the `rs2` register field. Under the RISC-V Svinval extension specification, `sfence.inval.ir` is encoded as funct12 = 12'b000110000001 (0x181), funct3 = 3'b000, opcode = 7'b1110011 (SYSTEM), with rd = x0 and rs1 = x0. It has NO `rs2` operand. Bit 20 is bit 0 of the funct12 opcode distinguishing `sfence.inval.ir` (0x181) from `sfence.w.inval` (0x180). Because bit 20 is 1, `~|InstrM[24:20]` unconditionally evaluates to 0. Consequently, `sfencevmaAllM` is permanently 0 whenever `sfence.inval.ir` executes. In `src/mmu/tlb/tlbcamline.sv` line 116, the flush condition is:
     assign ShouldFlush = TLBFlush & (~PTE_G | TLBFlushAll);
   Because `TLBFlushAll` is 0, `ShouldFlush` reduces to `TLBFlush & ~PTE_G`. Any global translation (PTE_G == 1) resident in the ITLB or DTLB is completely ignored and survives the fence intact.

2. Missing Pipeline Flush and PC Redirect (src/ieu/controller.sv line 353):
   In `src/ieu/controller.sv` lines 353-354:
     assign SFenceVmaD = PrivilegedD & (InstrD[31:25] == 7'b0001001);
     assign FenceD = SFenceVmaD | FenceXD;
   `SFenceVmaD` only decodes standard `sfence.vma` (funct7 `7'b0001001`). It completely omits all Svinval instructions (`sinval.vma` `7'b0001011`, `sfence.w.inval` `7'b0001100`, `sfence.inval.ir` `7'b0001100`). Consequently, `FenceD`, `FenceE`, `FenceM`, and `CSRWriteFenceM = CSRWriteM | FenceM` are never asserted for `sfence.inval.ir`. In `src/hazard/hazard.sv`, `FlushDCause`, `FlushECause`, and `FlushMCause` never fire, and in `src/ifu/ifu.sv` line 366, `pcmux2` never redirects instruction fetch to `NextValidPCE`. Older prefetched instructions continue executing without being flushed and refetched.

This violates the RISC-V Privileged Architecture Specification (v20211203) Chapter on the Svinval Extension, which mandates that `sfence.inval.ir` synchronizes all subsequent instruction fetches with preceding page table modifications across all address spaces, including global translations.
